      "key": "SFCC-196",
      "summary": "PDP UI – Maximum Purchase Quantity",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want\n to be clearly informed when I've reached the maximum purchase limit for a product,\nso that\n I understand why I can't add more to my bag.\nScreenshot (Figma is leading): \nSFCC enforces a configurable maximum purchase quantity per product and/or customer group, applied at the variant level (per size/colour)\n.\n Since the PDP has no quantity selector, enforcement is triggered when a shopper clicks Add to Bag multiple times for the same size. The system tracks how many units of the same variant are already in the shopper's bag and prevents addition beyond the configured limit. When the limit is reached, an inline message is displayed.",
