content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "17901",
  "key": "SFCC-51",
  "summary": "Promotional Announcement Banner UI",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n**I want** to see a promotional announcement banner, \n**so that** I am informed of current promotions, offers, or announcements as I browse the site.\n\nReference image (Figma is leading):\n\n![\"image-20260618-040246.png\"](image-20260618-040246.png)\n\n----\n\nThe promotional announcement banner is a thin full-width bar displayed above the global header on all devices but select pages as per configuration.\n\n  - **Page configuration:* The banner needs to be configurable per page (e.g. it may display on Home / PDP / PLP, but it does not on Z.immerse).\n  - **Position flexibility:* The banner needs to be configurable per page on what position it needs to appear (e.g. Top of page on home page or below navigation).\n  - **Rotating behaviour:* The banner supports multiple messages that rotate automatically. Each message can include text and an optional CTA link.\n  - **Content dependency:* Banner copy and rotation configuration is managed in Contentful. The component can be built with mock content prior to Contentful content model being finalised (contentful out of scope)",
  "status": {
    "name": "Blocked",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13363",
      "body": "Hey User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d - Just reviewing this and some clear ACs, very well written!\n\nAlso a few questions for technical implementation:\n\n1. For the 3 seconds between messages\n  1. This may need to be revisited given Screen Readers will need to time to get to this and read it out loud. \n  1. if on auto-rotation, the developers need to consider aria labels to notify screen readers of new content\n1. Are there controls to see multiple pages and to pause/play the auto-rotation? \n  1. This is generally an accessibility issue with auto playing of carousels - we can likely introduce CSS to stop animations for people with assisted browsers, but also would mean they would need controls and keyboard navigation.\n1. If there are multiple messages, does clicking the x icon close all messages, or just the visible one?\n1. When a user clicks the x icon, and the next time they load the page, do these messages come back or is there a cookie/session the devs need to add to ensure the message is not persisted?\n1. For this being a Contenful managed element, the team needs to do a **Technical Solution Design** and POC on how we integrate the Business Manager properties to Contenful and call those on the component rendering\n1. As this will be a component in the Contenful Studio builder, users can drag-n-drop where this lives on specific pages, but if this is going to live on a PLP and/or PDP or Global across all but Zimmerse, then will likely need a configuration to target specific SFCC Category IDs and Product IDs.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-07T09:14:03.842+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-07T09:14:03.842+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13385",
      "body": "User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 Thanks for this review! \nI’ve asked Dani for some input, and we’ve come to these conclusions: \n\n1. Rotation time should be configurable and depends on the length of the message. The duration needs to be adjusted to cover the message. So 3 seconds is definitely not fixed, I’ll update that in the AC. \n1. With regards to Pause, does the 'x' as Close button not cover the ability that one must be able to stop this rotating element from happening?\n1. Can confirm ‘x' will close all messages in the banner, not just the one currently displayed. I’ll update AC. \n1. If that banner is displayed in any other pages, it will remain closed if the user has used ‘x' to close it already in that session, so we do need to find a way to ensure it’s not persisted. I’ll update AC.\n1. Yes, created spike for that in sprint 1.\n1. User:712020:08a6f120-c836-4f71-92db-c97999401c49 think this one is relevant for the TSD as well. This banner is def currently available on PLP and PDP pages.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-09T12:07:49.830+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-09T12:07:49.830+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13386",
      "body": "Changed the AC after sign off - good to check once more on Tuesday with Emma/Rebecca.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-09T12:26:28.280+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-09T12:26:28.280+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13387",
      "body": "Following up from the thread above — proposing AC updates so this is ready to automate (Gherkin/Zephyr). Rotation timing is now a configurable per-message duration rather than a calculated value, and persistence is cookie-based, so updating 2 and 6 accordingly, plus adding new ACs for category/product targeting and accessibility.\n\n**Proposed AC updates:**\n\n1. Given the promotional banner is configured with multiple messages, when the page loads, then each message is displayed for a configurable duration (in seconds, set per message in Contentful) before automatically rotating to the next message in the configured sequence.\n\n1. Given a shopper closes the banner by clicking 'x', when they navigate to another page or reload within the same browser session, then a cookie records the closed state and the banner remains hidden site-wide until the cookie expires or is cleared.\n\n1. *(new)* Given the promotional banner is placed on a PDP or PLP via Contentful Studio, when it is configured with one or more SFCC Category IDs and/or Product IDs, then the banner is only displayed when the shopper is viewing a matching category or product page.\n\n1. *(new, draft)* Given a shopper is navigating via keyboard, when they tab through the page, then the banner's CTA link and close ('x') control each receive visible focus in a logical order and are operable via Enter/Space.\n\n1. *(new, draft — pending the open question below)* Given the banner auto-rotates between messages, when a new message displays, then the change is announced to assistive technology via an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, without interrupting the user's current screen reader focus.\n\n**Open question — play/pause:**\n\nClosing the banner removes it entirely for the session, but WCAG 2.2 SC 2.2.2 (Pause, Stop, Hide) requires auto-updating content running longer than 5 seconds to be pausable without being dismissed outright. Do we want a distinct pause-on-hover/focus (a common accessible pattern) or a dedicated pause control, separate from close? This also determines whether AC 9 needs a \"pause on focus/hover\" clause added.\n\nSquad ownership for test tagging will be confirmed at sprint planning — not blocking on that here.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-09T12:56:37.971+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-09T12:56:37.971+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13388",
      "body": "**Questions for next week’s refinement:**\n\n- Showing the banner on PDP/PLP - would it ever be a specific category / product and others not? Or is it: it either shows on all PLPs / all PDPs or none?\n- Is the banner global, except on Zimmerse? Can we get some information on the rules - where to show and where not to show, even though we understand it must be flexible - it may impact the way we design it if we can get a bit more info on this\n- Get thoughts on having a distinct pause-on-hover or dedicated pause control separate from close for accessibility - see Tim’s comment below.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-09T15:00:39.269+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-09T15:00:39.269+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13400",
      "body": "- Design team needs to show:\n      - Pause on hover (not yet designed - motion design) / Stop / Hide\n      - Position on the page - above and below the header\n- Showing the banner on PDP/PLP - would it ever be a specific category / product and others not? Or is it: it either shows on all PLPs / all PDPs or none?\n      - If we can have it, yes. Specific SKUs or collections",
      "author": {
